  "id": "COMPOUND:28091 - PROTEIN:4900",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Ircinialactam C appears to exert its biological effects by targeting the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, which is a key player in the transport of ions across cell membranes. This transporter is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including 5,7-Dihydroxy-8-methylchromone, Citronellal, and 6-Acetyl-2,2-dimethyl-8-(3-methyl-2-butenyl)-2H-1-benzopyran, all of which ultimately interact with Melanocyte protein PMEL. The evidence suggests a consistent pathway where Ent-Ircinialactam C modulates the activity of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, which in turn influences the expression or function of PMEL. The observed scores across the different paths indicate a plausible mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same intermediate (H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3) supports the hypothesis that Ent-Ircinialactam C may exert its effects through a shared pathway involving this transporter. The integration of these findings suggests that Ent-Ircinialactam C could potentially influence melanocyte function by modulating ion transport, which may have implications for melanogenesis and related processes.",
